    survivingLiens: "A California tax deed conveys free of most liens existing before the sale, but federal tax liens survive (IRS 120-day post-sale redemption right), as do taxes/assessments that become payable after the sale. County notices also flag that some bonds/assessments levied by other agencies may remain — verify parcel-by-parcel under R&T §3712.",
    quietTitle: "Not a statutory prerequisite, but practically required — most California title insurers will not insure tax-deed property without quiet title (often 3–6 months; commonly wait ~1 year after deed recording).",
