    survivingLiens: "Upset Sale: mortgages, judgments, and many private liens typically survive — bid accordingly. Judicial Sale: sold free and clear of most liens after proper lienholder notice (federal tax liens still need analysis). Always search records before bidding.",
    quietTitle: "Upset titles are often uninsurable without further proceedings; Judicial Sale titles are cleaner but insurers may still want quiet title or waiting periods depending on notice history.",
    gisMap: { label: "Bucks County GIS / parcel viewer", url: "https://www.buckscounty.gov/" },
