    notes: "Texas redeemable tax deed county. Fort Bend does not sell tax lien certificates. Delinquent taxes are judicially foreclosed; Constables conduct public auctions (typically first Tuesday of each month, 10 a.m.–4 p.m., moving to first Wednesday if Tuesday is Jan 1 or July 4). Multiple precinct Constables and contracted delinquent-tax counsel (Linebarger, Perdue Brandon, Coats Rose, Smith Murdaugh, etc.) post lists. Sales recently held at Gus George Law Enforcement Academy — Patton Hall, Richmond (verify location each month). Post-sale statutory redemption: generally 2 years for homestead/agricultural/mineral, 180 days for other property (Texas Tax Code Ch. 34).",
    auctionFormat: "In-person",
    auctionPlatform: { label: "Fort Bend County Constables — Property / Tax Sales", url: "https://www.fortbendcountytx.gov/government/departments/constables/property-sales" },
    auctionFrequency: "First Tuesday of each month (as parcels are posted); confirm precinct lists monthly",
    depositRules: "No typical advance online deposit. Highest bidders pay in full same day (often by 2:00 p.m. at the Constable’s office) in cash, cashier’s check, or money order payable to the specific Constable/precinct. Separate certified funds per property; no change given. Confirm precinct-specific terms on that Constable’s sale page.",
